@host = http://localhost:5300

### A city
GET {{host}}/api/cities/1

### Invalid id: GetCityQuery's [Range], checked before the handler runs
### 400 validation_failed, validationErrors keyed id
GET {{host}}/api/cities/0

### Not found: the handler's declared CityNotFound, its id in details
### 404 atlas_1001, details { cityId: 99 }
GET {{host}}/api/cities/99

### Invalid: the use case's own rules, validated before the handler runs
### 400 validation_failed, validationErrors keyed name, countryCode, population, districts[0].population
POST {{host}}/api/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "countryCode": "ua", "population": 0, "districts": [{ "name": "Podil", "population": -1 }] }

### Created: 201, Location /api/cities/{id}
POST {{host}}/api/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Lviv", "countryCode": "UA", "population": 717273, "districts": null }

### Conflict: the handler's declared CityNameTaken, with the id of the city that has the name
### 409 atlas_1002, details { cityId: 1 }
POST {{host}}/api/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Kyiv", "countryCode": "UA", "population": 1, "districts": null }

### What reached a handler, and how it ended
GET {{host}}/audit
